## JOIN NODE — verified from Sample 2 (JOIN1) and Sample 1
===========================================================================
action = "join". sources = [leftNodeName, rightNodeName].

```json
"JOIN1": {
  "action": "join",
  "parameters": {
    "joinType": "LEFT_OUTER",
    "leftKeys":  ["cgcloud__Account__c", "ProductId", "ForecastDateString"],
    "rightKeys": ["cgcloud__Account__c", "ProductId", "ForecastDateString"],
    "rightQualifier": "NonPromo"
  },
  "sources": ["FILTER0", "DROP_FIELDS4"]
}
```

VERIFIED joinType values (UPPERCASE_SNAKE — NOT title case):
  "LEFT_OUTER"   ← keep all left rows (most common for enrichment)
  "LOOKUP"       ← enrich (from Sample 1)
  Other API values: "INNER", "RIGHT_OUTER", "CROSS" (not seen in samples — verify before use)

  DO NOT USE title case ("LeftOuter", "Lookup") — the API schema doc lists those
  but the runtime rejects them. Use UPPERCASE_SNAKE as the deployed samples do.

KEY FACTS (verified against samples):
  - leftKeys / rightKeys are ARRAYS (can be multi-key composite joins).
  - rightQualifier is present; leftQualifier is NOT used in the samples — omit it
    unless a validate error explicitly asks for it.
  - After join, right-side fields are prefixed: NonPromo.FieldName.
  - Rename/drop right-side fields DOWNSTREAM using a schema node (see below).
  - sources[0] = left (driving) node, sources[1] = right (lookup) node.

