## SCHEMA NODE — rename / drop fields (verified from Sample 1)
===========================================================================
action = "schema". This is how you RENAME fields after a join (not rightQualifier
formula tricks). Two operation shapes:

RENAME (EDIT_ATTRIBUTES-style — set newProperties.name + .label):
```json
"EDIT_ATTRIBUTES25": {
  "action": "schema",
  "parameters": {
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "SUM_Predicted_SalesUnits",
        "newProperties": {
          "name": "Predicted_Baseline_SalesUnits",
          "label": "Predicted Baseline SalesUnits"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "sources": ["<previous node>"]
}
```

DROP fields: use a schema node whose fields carry a drop flag, OR the join's own
schema.slice. In Sample recipes, dropping is done with dedicated DROP_FIELDS schema
nodes — read Sample 1 for the exact drop shape when you need it.

Node naming convention in samples: schema nodes are named by function —
EDIT_ATTRIBUTES25, DROP_FIELDS4 — but the action is always "schema".

