## AGGREGATE NODE — verified from Sample 2 (AGGREGATE1)
===========================================================================
action = "aggregate".

```json
"AGGREGATE1": {
  "action": "aggregate",
  "parameters": {
    "aggregations": [
      { "action": "SUM", "name": "SUM_Amount",  "label": "Sum of Amount",  "source": "Amount" },
      { "action": "COUNT", "name": "Row_Count",  "label": "Row Count",      "source": "Id" }
    ],
    "groupings": ["cgcloud__Account__c", "ProductId", "ForecastDateString"],
    "nodeType": "STANDARD",
    "pivots": []
  },
  "sources": ["<previous node>"]
}
```

VERIFIED (UPPERCASE — NOT title case):
  aggregations[].action: "SUM", "COUNT", "AVG", "MAX", "MIN", "UNIQUE" (uppercase).
    (API doc says "Sum"/"Count" — WRONG at runtime. Samples use "SUM"/"COUNT".)
  nodeType: "STANDARD" (uppercase). NOT "Standard".
  groupings: array of field-name strings.
  pivots: [] (present, usually empty).
  aggregations[].source = input field name.

CONDITIONAL aggregation (SUM only Won opps): the aggregate node has no WHERE.
  Pattern used in samples: a FORMULA node BEFORE aggregate creates a numeric flag
  (e.g. Won_Amount = case when IsWon = 'true' then Amount else 0 end), then SUM that.

