## LOAD NODE — two forms
===========================================================================
action = "load", sources = [].

FORM A — load a SAVED dataset (dataset-to-dataset, verified from samples):
```json
"parameters": {
  "dataset": { "type": "analyticsDataset", "name": "Forecast_Dataset4", "label": "..." },
  "fields": [],
  "sampleDetails": { "type": "TopN", "sortBy": [] }
}
```

FORM B — load a SALESFORCE OBJECT via SFDC_LOCAL (connectedDataset).
The samples don't include this form (they chain datasets), so use the shape the org
uses. Confirmed working shape:
```json
"parameters": {
  "dataset": { "type": "connectedDataset", "label": "Opportunity" }
}
```
type "connectedDataset" is REQUIRED for object loads or the API returns JSON_PARSER_ERROR.
If a connectedDataset load fails, get-recipe on an existing org recipe that loads
a Salesforce object and mirror its exact dataset block.

