## computeRelative NODE — window functions lag/lead/row_number (from Sample 2)
===========================================================================
action = "computeRelative". Use for prior-period values, running calcs, sequencing.
```json
"parameters": {
  "expressionType": "SQL",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "ForecastSalesUnitsW-1",
      "label": "ForecastSalesUnitsW-1",
      "type": "NUMBER",
      "precision": 10, "scale": 2,
      "formulaExpression": "lag(Final_Forecast_SaleUnits)",
      "defaultValue": ""
    }
  ],
  "orderBy": [{ "fieldName": "Forecast_Date", "direction": "ASC" }],
  "partitionBy": ["AccountProductKey"]
}
```
Verified functions: lag(field), lead(field), row_number().
expressionType here is "SQL" (uppercase) — note this differs from formula nodes;
mirror the sample exactly per node type.

