## TYPECAST NODE — convert a field's type  [ORG-VERIFIED 2026-09-06]
===========================================================================
Built + ran on storm-org: converted Account.NumberOfEmployees (int) → NUMBER measure,
which then summed correctly (83,960). action = "typeCast".
Uses newProperties.typeProperties — NOT a flat "type" key (flat type → JSON_PARSER_ERROR).
```json
"TYPECAST0": {
  "action": "typeCast",
  "parameters": {
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "NumberOfEmployees",
        "newProperties": {
          "label": "Employees Measure",
          "name": "Employees_Measure",
          "typeProperties": { "precision": 18, "scale": 0, "type": "NUMBER" }
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "sources": ["LOAD_ACCOUNT"]
}
```
typeProperties.type: NUMBER (with precision+scale), TEXT, DATE_ONLY, DATE_TIME.
Common use: text-that-should-be-a-measure → NUMBER so it can be summed/averaged in dashboards.

