## appendV2 NODE — union two branches (SQL UNION)  [ORG-VERIFIED 2026-09-06]
===========================================================================
Built + ran on storm-org: unioned 21 Enterprise + 25 Mid-Market Account rows into one dataset.
action = "appendV2". Uses fieldMappings with top/bottom (NOT a sources array in parameters).
sources[0] = top branch, sources[1] = bottom branch.
```json
"APPEND0": {
  "action": "appendV2",
  "parameters": {
    "fieldMappings": [
      { "top": "Id",   "bottom": "Id" },
      { "top": "Name", "bottom": "Name" },
      { "top": "Type", "bottom": "Type" },
      { "top": "Employees_Measure", "bottom": "Employees_Measure" }
    ]
  },
  "sources": ["FILTER_BRANCH_A", "FILTER_BRANCH_B"]
}
```
- fieldMappings maps top-branch field → bottom-branch field (names can differ across branches).
- List every field you want in the union output. Unmapped fields are dropped.
- For disjoint schemas, the Sample also shows enableDisjointedSchemaMerge — but plain fieldMappings
  is the proven simple case.

