## VERIFIED PATTERN — Aggregate after Join-then-Schema: join reps BEFORE aggregate so name fields are in groupings
VERIFIED DS_Sales_Rep_Performance: When aggregating by rep name + manager name, join User tables BEFORE the AGGREGATE node so Rep_Name/Manager_Name are available as grouping dimensions. Pattern: LOAD_OPP → FORMULA chain → JOIN_REP → JOIN_MGR → SCHEMA (rename Owner.Name→Rep_Name, Mgr.Name→Manager_Name) → AGGREGATE (groupings: [OwnerId, Rep_Name, Manager_Name, FiscalYear, FiscalQuarter]) → post-agg FORMULA (Win_Rate, Pipeline_Coverage) → OUTPUT. FiscalYear from SFDC_LOCAL is a NUMBER field — treat as measure in SAQL (cannot group by it directly in query-dataset).


